{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"wc -l review-inputs/*.md src/yin/vm/semantic/{rows,frame,layout,engine,semantic,driver,export,ffi}.cljc; rg -n '\"'^##|''^###'\"' review-inputs/1793650000000-architect-6d-plan-v2.report.md\"","aggregated_output":"wc: src/yin/vm/semantic/rows.cljc: open: No such file or directory\nwc: src/yin/vm/semantic/frame.cljc: open: No such file or directory\nwc: src/yin/vm/semantic/layout.cljc: open     156 review-inputs/1792135181000-architect-6d-plan-second-review.report.md\n      10 review-inputs/1792141480000-architect-6d-plan-v2-mob-codex.prompt.md\n      10 review-inputs/1792141480000-architect-6d-plan-v2-mob-glm.prompt.md\n      10 review-inputs/1792141480000-architect-6d-plan-v2-mob-muse.prompt.md\n     639 review-inputs/1793650000000-architect-6d-plan-v2.report.md\n     825 total\n: No such file or directory\nwc: src/yin/vm/semantic/engine.cljc: open: No such file or directory\nwc: src/yin/vm/semantic/semantic.cljc: open: No such file or directory\nwc: src/yin/vm/semantic/driver.cljc: open: No such file or directory\nwc: src/yin/vm/semantic/export.cljc: open: No such file or directory\nwc: src/yin/vm/semantic/ffi.cljc: open: No such file or directory\n27:## 1. The nine findings, verified\n31:### F1 — ready-queue exception contradicts any-pc migration: ACCEPTED (reproduced)\n48:### F2 — R0 rejects a state the scheduler constructs: ACCEPTED (reproduced)\n63:### F3 — fuel does not bound an install child or the program tick: ACCEPTED\n67:### F4 — a tenure failure loses the just-computed boundary: ACCEPTED\n71:### F5 — the all-pc stack equation is false: ACCEPTED (reproduced)\n87:### F6 — grant-check instruction wrong: ACCEPTED\n91:### F7 — the primitive refusal predicate is broader than L(pc): ACCEPTED\n95:### F8 — harness order compares the wrong state and mutates its fixture: ACCEPTED\n99:### F9 — the document text overstates and the inventory is incomplete: ACCEPTED\n107:## 2. What v1 got wrong, plainly\n125:## 3. Plan v2\n127:### 3.1 State model: the task-state product\n192:### 3.2 Lift, lower, restore (`rows.cljc`, `layout.cljc` `state-prim`)\n207:### 3.3 Custody and lifecycle of a running root\n222:### 3.4 Fuel and budget propagation\n243:### 3.5 Stack layouts at control-flow pcs; the register side\n259:### 3.6 Harness order, worlds, oracle, coverage\n269:### 3.7 Amended document text (exact)\n273:#### 3.7.1 `yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md`\n357:#### 3.7.2 `yin.vm.semantic.md` (frozen design)\n373:#### 3.7.3 `yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md`\n403:#### 3.7.4 `yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md`\n407:#### 3.7.5 `yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md` §7 (`:560-579`)\n413:#### 3.7.6 `yin.vm.linker.dht.md` §14.1\n417:#### 3.7.7 `yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md`\n421:#### 3.7.8 The assessment's §F and the gap list\n427:### 3.8 Complete inventory of safepoint-only assertions\n523:### 3.9 Slices, order, parallelism, effort\n542:#### 6d-a: the reference lane\n569:#### 6d-b: holder, custody, expiry, recovery\n582:#### 6e: the cross-engine half\n590:#### Effort\n604:### 3.10 Decisions for the owner (defaults stated so 6d-a can start)\n615:### 3.11 Risks\n627:## 4. Verification honesty\n635:## 5. Readiness\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
